# This repo is driven by `airlock-dev-orch`

- Design, specification, and implementation work happens in `../airlock-dev-orch`.
  `cd` there and run the spec or code graph — do not start it here.
- Non-trivial changes need an RFC in `../airlock-dev-orch/docs/rfc/`, reviewed by a
  second agent and approved by a human.
- Trivial fixes (typo, comment, formatting) may be made here, on a
  `<tool>/<model>/<feature>` branch, naming the `trivial` exemption in the PR.
- **Building and testing here is always fine** — this repo is self-contained:
  `mise install && make check` works with no orchestrator on disk. Nothing in
  the build may reference `../airlock-dev-orch`.
- Never commit to the default branch. Linear history, PRs only, rebase merge.
- Add commits in response to review; **never force-push** without explicit
  human permission.
- `make fmt` and `make lint` clean before every commit; commits carry an `RFC:`
  footer and a `Co-Authored-By` trailer for this tool
  (`Co-Authored-By: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`).
- A human approves and merges every PR. No agent does.
